WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.000
EPA 608 is not optional. You cannot legally touch refrigerant without it. Let's
make sure you pass.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:20.000
EPA 608 has four certification types. Type I covers small appliances (5 lbs or
less). Type II covers high-pressure systems (R-410A, R-22, R-134a). Type III
covers low-pressure systems (R-11, R-123 chillers). Universal certification

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Here are the key terms. Write these down.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Universal Certification: Passes all four EPA 608 sections. Allows work on any
refrigerant system type.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:50.000
Type I: Small appliances — factory-charged systems with 5 lbs or less.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Type II: High-pressure systems — residential and commercial AC, heat pumps.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:10.000
Here's why this matters on the job: Get Universal. Type II alone limits your
career. Universal opens every door — residential, commercial, industrial.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:20.000
Watch out for these: Core section is required for ALL certification types. And
certification does not expire but keep your card.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:30.000
Quick check: what is the maximum fine for knowingly venting refrigerant? If you
don't know that number, go back and read it again.

